# nodus/oevm/tests/target/liveness-fastpoll.env — rete#273 D1's reproduce-first gate
#
# A 100 ms timer beside a 3 s blocking reaction every 4 s. RED on the pre-#273 build
# (the observer judges 100 x 8 = 800 ms and reboots the node inside its first slow
# tick: boot 2 reports `not ok 1 no reboot note`, cond=pulse-undrained deadline=800ms
# in the archive). GREEN on the declared rule (appCad 6000: 20 slow ticks, pass=2, no
# reboot through the observation window). A 1.5 s block did NOT reproduce the red
# (2026-09-17): the old rule samples at 1000 ms and needs two in-block samples.
#
# The red was RUN AND ARCHIVED on 2026-09-17 with the pre-Task-1 VM sources
# (bb26b32's src/, zephyr/src/ and kernel.nsl) checked out under HEAD's harness:
# archive porta-v1-final-1241-g1e6f921-dirty-20260917T181643, console
# console-c6spare-2026-09-17.log 18:16:56 -07:00 —
#   oevm: WEDGE cond=pulse-undrained overdue=201ms deadline=800ms up=6023ms pending=1
#   TAP fastpoll not ok 1 no reboot note THE OBSERVER FIRED ON A HEALTHY NODE
# then a reboot every ~7 s. The green followed the same day on the fixed build
# (porta-v1-final-1241-g1e6f921-dirty-20260917T181834): 50 slow ticks in ~200 s,
# zero WEDGE lines, pass=2 fail=0. A gate that starts by reproducing the defect
# is the only kind that can tell "fixed" from "never broken".
#
# No radio, no bridge: nothing here needs CONF_EXTRA. class=disruptive because the
# pre-fix build reboots the board.
SCENARIO=liveness-fastpoll
TAP_NAME=fastpoll
NODE=FastPollProbeC6.nsl
BOARD_ID=esp32c6
CLASS=disruptive
TIMEOUT_S=240
OBSERVE_S=120
OBSERVE_PROGRESS='^.*fastpoll tick [0-9]+'
